{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "זרחה", :translit "zar'chah", :gloss "[it] shone"} {:he "והשמש זרחה", :translit "veha-shemesh zar'chah", :gloss "and the sun shone"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word זרחה appears in our verse and again in Exodus 22:2 (והשמש זרחה); Ba'al HaTurim flags the verbal link between the two adjacent verses."}], :frame {:text "Both occurrences of זרחה appear in adjacent verses dealing with the thief (Exodus 22:1–2), so Ba'al HaTurim ties them together contextually.", :sources ["Exodus 22:2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "על המים וגו' אדומים כדם", :translit "al ha-mayim vegomer adumim ka-dam", :gloss "upon the waters […] red as blood"} {:he "שמש זרחה ונודד", :translit "shemesh zar'chah ve-noded", :gloss "sun shone and [he] departed"} {:he "והצרעת זרחה במצחו", :translit "ve-ha-tzara'at zar'chah be-mitz'cho", :gloss "and the tzara'at shone on his forehead"} {:he "זרחה עליו השמש", :translit "zar'chah alav ha-shemesh", :gloss "the sun shone upon him"} {:he "אדומים כדם", :translit "adumim ka-dam", :gloss "red as blood"} {:he "וזרחה לכם יראי שמי", :translit "ve-zar'chah lakhem yerei shemi", :gloss "and it shall shine for you who fear My name"} {:he "ומרפא בכנפיה", :translit "u-marpah be-kanafeha", :gloss "and healing in its wings"} {:he "הנה יום בא בוער כתנור וגו' ולהט אותם וגו'", :translit "hineh yom ba bo'er ka-tanur vegomer velahat otam vegomer", :gloss "Behold a day comes burning like an oven […] and it shall burn them […]"} {:he "זרחה לו", :translit "zar'chah lo", :gloss "[it] shone for him / upon him"} {:he "והשמש זרחה", :translit "veha-shemesh zar'chah", :gloss "and the sun shone"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah: links זרחה in our verse to על המים אדומים כדם (2 Kings 3:22) — if the sun has risen the thief owes blood-money."} {:kind :other, :note "Second gezerah shavah: links זרחה to וזרחה לכם יראי שמי (Malachi 3:20), where the sun heals the righteous but burns the wicked."}], :frame {:text "The law in Exodus 22:2 distinguishes between a thief killed before dawn (no blood-money) and one killed after sunrise (blood-money owed). Ba'al HaTurim builds the halakhic threshold from 2 Kings 3:22, where water appears אדומים כדם in the morning light — the shining sun produces 'blood.' Separately, Malachi 3:20 says the sun of redemption brings ומרפא בכנפיה for the God-fearing, while Malachi 3:19 warns הנה יום בא בוער כתנור — the same solar imagery heals the righteous and burns the wicked. He reads והשמש זרחה and זרחה לו (2 Kings 3:22) through both lenses: sunlight can yield blood-guilt or healing depending on the recipient.", :sources ["Exodus 22:2" "2 Kings 3:22" "Malachi 3:20" "Malachi 3:19"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Word זרחה appears in our verse and again in Exodus 22:2 (והשמש זרחה); Ba'al HaTurim flags the verbal link between the two adjacent verses.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah: links זרחה in our verse to על המים אדומים כדם (2 Kings 3:22) — if the sun has risen the thief owes blood-money.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Second gezerah shavah: links זרחה to וזרחה לכם יראי שמי (Malachi 3:20), where the sun heals the righteous but burns the wicked.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:18:32.570171764Z", :model "glm-5.2"}